{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nexp={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"f47677cc0dd94647aa374fc84b1e6b8e-question-1\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"epaxos/assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"execution_package\\\":\\\"./epaxos\\\",\n \\\"test_names\\\":[\\\"TestAssuranceEPaxosRecoveryBallotNonOwnerBoundary\\\"],\n \\\"anchors\\\":[{\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-decl-recovery\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"startRecoveryForInstance\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1127,\\\"end_line\\\":1141},\n            {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-decl-prepare-reply\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1204,\\\"end_line\\\":1235}],\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-makeballot\\\",\\\"s-decl-recovery\\\",\\\"s-decl-prepare-reply\\\",\\\"s-isleader-default\\\",\\\"s-betheleader\\\",\\\"s-exec-recovery-trigger\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Same 5-replica harness as the recovery-ballot experiment. Owner replica 0 proposes X on instance (0,0) and enters the Accept phase at ballot 0 towards replicas 2 and 3 (replica 1's non-equal reply is delivered first and replica 1 then fails); replica 0's AcceptReplies are left in flight; replica 2 then recovers the instance at its own ballot 7, so the accepting peers store bal 7, and replica 2 fails after broadcasting that Prepare. Two further recovery attempts are then made at replica 1 and replica 3, whose fixed ballots for a non-owned instance are 6 and 8 respectively, and each attempt's Prepare/PrepareReply traffic and follow-up messages are recorded.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"Same construction, transport boundary and crash model as the value-adoption and recovery-ballot experiments; in-process replicas, marshaled RPC structs decoded per delivery, FIFO per link, no delivery to crashed replicas.\\\",\n   \\\"The two recoverers hold the instance (replica 1 pre-accepted X and answered the owner's Prepare; replica 3 received the owner's Accept), which is what lets their executors act on it.\\\",\n   \\\"No production logic is modified; IsLeader stays false for both recoverers.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No client path, no state-machine execution, no run() loop or recovery timer loop in the harness.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"n\\\":5,\\\"f\\\":2,\\\"owner\\\":0,\\\"first_recoverer\\\":2,\\\"below_recoverer\\\":1,\\\"above_recoverer\\\":3,\\\"stored_ballot\\\":7,\\\"non_owner_ballots\\\":[6,8]}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness drives the owner's proposal and accept phase through the target's own path, delivers replica 2's higher-ballot Prepare so the peers store bal 7 and then fails replica 2, and finally calls startRecoveryForInstance(0,0) first at replica 1 and then at replica 3, delivering each attempt's Prepare/PrepareReply traffic through handlePrepare/handlePrepareReply and recording tried, matching and follow-up messages.\\\",\n \\\"requirement\\\":\\\"Recovery must be attainable by any replica that holds the instance: a recovering replica whose fixed ballot is below the ballot the accepting peers have stored must still be able to advance the instance, either by a prepared quorum and a sub-case dispatch or by a later attempt using a ballot above the stored one.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"The target's own ballot policy (epaxos/epaxos.go:439-451 makeBallot) and its rejection handling (epaxos/epaxos.go:1204-1235 handlePrepareReply): the peers answer honestly with the ballot they stored and the recoverers are ordinary replicas.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"owner-accepted\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"instance_state\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"phase\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"after_preaccept_replies\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"cmd_op\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"peers-store-high-ballot\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"instance_state\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"phase\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"after_high_ballot_prepare\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"bal\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":7}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"round-start-below\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"round_start\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"stored_bal_before_attempt\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":7}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"round-start-above\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"round_start\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"stored_bal_before_attempt\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":7}]}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"recovery_attempt\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"replica\\\",\\\"instance_row\\\",\\\"instance_index\\\",\\\"round\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"round-start-below\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"recovery_advanced\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"stored_bal_before_attempt\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":7}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A non-owner recoverer whose fixed ballot (6) is below the peers' stored ballot (7) still advances the instance: no matching reply and no follow-up message means the attempt is inert; violated in this configuration.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"recovery_attempt\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"replica\\\",\\\"instance_row\\\",\\\"instance_index\\\",\\\"round\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"round-start-above\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"recovery_advanced\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"stored_bal_before_attempt\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":7}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: a non-owner recoverer whose fixed ballot (8) is above the peers' stored ballot (7) produces matching replies and dispatches its phase-1 proposal; expected to hold, locating the boundary at the comparison between the recoverer's fixed ballot and the stored ballot.\\\"}]\n}\njson.dump({\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Requested execution of a probe that measures the boundary stated as a limitation of the recovery-authority finding: the same instance is recovered first by a non-owner whose fixed ballot is below the peers' stored ballot and then by a non-owner whose fixed ballot is above it.\\\",\\\"experiment\\\":exp},open('draft/update19.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission update19.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
